      hu: "A Jeonju Hanok Falu egy hagyományos koreai falu, több mint 800 hanok házzal, amelyek hagyományos stílusban épültek. Jeonju város központjában található, amely híres kulináris kultúrájáról. A falu betekintést nyújt a Joseon-korba kulturális workshopokkal, teaházakkal és kézműves boltokkal. A hanji (koreai papír) készítésének központja is. A híres Jeonju bibimbap innen származik. A falut évente több mint 10 millió turista látogatja.",
      ro: "Satul Hanok din Jeonju este un sat coreean tradițional cu peste 800 de case hanok, construite în stil tradițional. Este situat în centrul orașului Jeonju, cunoscut pentru cultura sa culinară. Satul oferă perspective asupra perioadei Joseon cu ateliere culturale, case de ceai și magazine de artizanat. Este, de asemenea, un centru pentru fabricarea hârtiei hanji. Faimosul Jeonju bibimbap își are originea aici. Satul atrage peste 10 milioane de turiști anual.",
      en: "Jeonju Hanok Village, located in Jeonju city, is a preserved area of over 800 traditional Korean houses (hanok) dating back to the Joseon Dynasty. The village covers an area of approximately 0.5 km². It is famous for its cultural heritage, including traditional tea ceremonies, paper-making (hanji), and Korean food, especially Jeonju bibimbap. The village also hosts the Jeonju International Film Festival. In 2016, Jeonju was designated as a City of Gastronomy by UNESCO.",
